amux inbox — questions and follow-ups waiting for you

usage: amux inbox [<command>]

Every pending question for the user, from any session, in one place, with
answers routed back to the asking session. Reading works from a host terminal,
the admin console and the overseer; answering, dismissing and acknowledging
are the user's alone (host terminal).

commands:
  ls [--all] [--json]  pending questions, global inbox counts and the workgroup summary (the default)
  answer <entry> [<text>...] [--choice <label>]... [--allow | --deny]
                       answer one entry; amux re-checks it is still open and delivers it
  dismiss <entry>      hide an entry (a live question is hidden until it changes)
  ack <item>           acknowledge a global-inbox item as the user (lets the overseer act on it)

Run 'amux inbox <command> --help' for details.
